WEBVTT

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.670
List.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.750
Don't Like:

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.380
People who are all talk

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.340
Grownups who are liars!

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.380
People who worry about appearances

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.800
Hypocrites who pretend to be fair

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.720
Myself! I hate myself!! Moron!!

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.180
Like:

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.350
Animals. Only the cute ones. Like cats.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.560
Milk tea. Lemon's okay, too.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.030
Black. Blue. And gray,
as long as it's dark.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.440
Also... Myself.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.450
How many times have I
told you not to read my stuff?

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.990
Why did you read it?
Are you a moron?!

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.120
It's just a memo anyway!

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.330
It's. Just. A. Memo!

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.000
Got that?

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.000
Okay, then come with me...

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.750
It's. Just. A. Memo!

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.520
So this is the comb you mentioned?

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.770
You're right, it is unusual.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.530
Do you want me to ask
Forensics to take a look?

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.530
They might find a clue.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.780
That's okay.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.860
Are you sure?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.280
Yes, I'm sure.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.790
My memories are important,
but I've decided to be patient.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.210
Here it comes!

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:58.960
The Guardian?

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.580
Want to try reeling him in?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.800
If I reeled in the Guardian, that would
be another memory, right?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.960
Of course!

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.010
I think I can see it!

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.750
Hey!

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.220
My memory got away.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.440
Sorry, I let my guard down.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.440
Huh? Something wrong?

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.270
Yosuke?

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.400
What about you, Hanamura-senpai?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.940
Is something the matter?

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.320
Yes! That's right! Please...

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.610
You guys, you gotta help me out!

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:33.450
If I don't act fast, I'll have to
transfer to another school!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.500
What?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.630
An on-stage event? Me?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.800
Please! It's the only way!

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:53.010
For me... for my old man... for Junes...
 Do us this favor, will you?

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.600
Hey, hold up a sec!

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:59.140
How does Rise-chan going
onstage help you and Junes?

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.400
We've got to draw a big
crowd, no matter what.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.730
All our plans got totally messed up...

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:09.150
Does this have anything to do with that event
at the Inaba Police Station that got canceled?

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.700
What do you mean?

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:16.830
This Sunday, the idol singer, Kanami Mashita was
supposed to serve as an honorary police chief...

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.330
Who's that?

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:29.880
Kanamin

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.170
An idol singer whose
star is currently on the rise.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:28.000
She's often touted as the one to watch
in the post-Rise Kujikawa era.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:33.260
And it's Kanamin's honorary police
chief event that they suddenly canceled...

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:39.270
I hear that the police didn't have time to prepare
for her because of that uproar when I went missing.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.180
I'm really sorry about that...

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.270
It's not your fault, Naoto.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:47.610
So what does that falling through
have to do with you, Hanamura-senpai?

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:52.490
We planned the sale to take advantage of
the crowd that would come for Kanamin,

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.860
so my dad's really in a jam now...

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.330
That's why you thought you could
draw a crowd if Rise-chan did a show?

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.950
You're telling me
to take Kanami's place?

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.710
So there's no way, huh?

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.670
My dad's being so nice,
for some reason.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.510
Would they really can
a store manager over this?

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:18.350
If that happens, then neither
of us can stay in this town...

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.770
That's what you meant by transferring.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.770
You mean you're not
going to be around anymore?

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.190
Just singing and handshakes.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.610
You're cool with it?

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.740
But with one condition.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:36.200
You all have to be onstage with me.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.870
Hey, what kind of twist
is that all of a sudden?

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:41.790
What do you think
you're gonna make us do?

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.120
Be my backup band, of course!

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.830
Band...

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:01.100
No sound's coming out.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.020
It must be broken, right?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.060
It's making this whooshing sound...

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.560
Think you can handle it?

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.490
Whoa...

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:15.740
You gotta be kidding me...

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.330
That's amazing!

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.580
Have you done this before?

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.000
You totally rock!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.500
That's awesome.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:30.170
All right, do you think
you can play this section?

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.260
What about the song you just played?

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.800
Now this.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.060
Why can't you play
anything but that?

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.690
How should I know?

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:51.150
By the way, what are these
tadpoles drawn all over this sheet?

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.650
Come to think of it, I can't
read sheet music at all.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.280
Me neither.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.780
I guess I'll be
transferring out then, huh?

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.330
Don't worry.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.910
When you transfer schools,
we're all going with you.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.580
Over my dead body.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.040
It's too soon for you to give up.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:10.920
About this song...

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.300
It actually repeats
the same pattern quite a lot.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.130
Melody A, melody B, chorus.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:19.340
It's all the same
pattern, repeated twice.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.890
Now that you mention it...

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:25.060
Also, the number of chords
used is actually quite paltry.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:27.480
Since you have experience,
Hanamura-senpai,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.150
and I can play up to a point,
I think we can pull it off.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.940
Just like a great detective!

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.110
Not that being a detective
has anything to do with it!

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:36.940
Naoto-kun!

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:37.900
What about me?

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.240
What should I do?

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:44.530
If you could both just nail that intro,
Satonaka-senpai and Amagi-senpai...

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.450
All right! Roger that!
I'm gonna get pumped up!

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.080
And I'll pump some sound out of this.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.540
Okay, that's the spirit.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.300
<i>Memories...</i>

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.050
<i>I've got to make them.</i>

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:08.680
Damn!

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.520
Just look at the time!

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:12.980
Don't worry!

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:14.730
I thought this might happen,

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.110
so I got permission to use
the Junes warehouse!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.740
Hanamura-senpai, you rock!

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:24.570
Okay, everyone bring their
instruments, and let's hit the road!

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.450
Right!

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.950
Band practice?

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:33.920
Yeah, he just called to tell me
that he'd be late because of that.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.630
I hear they're going to
do a concert at Junes.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:37.750
Oh, yeah?

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.720
Sounds like they're
enjoying their youth!

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:43.720
Is Big Bro gonna sing a song?

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.720
I want to go see him!

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.890
Sure, why not?
Want to go with me?

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.060
Yes!

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.310
Adachi, you coming, too?

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:54.440
I'll take a pass.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.310
What's this, you sure?

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:59.320
You've been pretty tight with
Yu these days, am I right?

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.990
You seem to be
hanging out with him a lot.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.160
Good work today, you guys!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.490
See you tomorrow!

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.160
Bye!

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.710
Yeah! See ya!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.830
Let's get something
to eat on our way home.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.460
Yeah, good idea!

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.210
What should we have?

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.920
I'm going to practice some more.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.340
Since I have the time.

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.510
But... where?

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.010
In the Velvet Room.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:35.400
The Nose kicked me out.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.940
Said I was too noisy.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:39.150
Reality sure bites, huh?

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:52.080
<i>Even if I ignore my uneasiness,
my heart feels blue</i>

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:58.170
<i>In the end, another morning
when I feel lost will dawn again</i>

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.090
Yu-senpai...

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.050
And Marie-chan! What are you...?

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.890
We thought we'd get in some
morning practice. You, too, Rise?

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.270
N-No...

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:15.190
I was just warming up
my voice, that's all.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.860
L-Let's get going!

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.940
It's a little early, but I'm sure
the others will be here soon!

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:23.110
Sure.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.570
One, two, three, four!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.100
W-Was that me?

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.650
It wasn't me, all right? After all,
this doesn't make any sound.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:08.950
Our cutting-edge, young audience
seeks unpredictability from music as well.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:10.990
A strange sound suddenly rings out!

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:12.330
And that is...

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.620
a sinful betrayal beyond
anyone's expectations.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:18.160
Can you feel it?

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:20.130
Oh, yeah, I feel it all right.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.630
"Teddie's the culprit!" 
That's what you mean, right?

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.710
Are we really gonna
get it together in time?

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:28.840
I'm starting to think we're
doomed no matter what.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:30.300
The moment you give up...

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.890
It's game over.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:33.890
Sensei!

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.640
I... I...

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:42.360
I want to be in the band!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.400
What kind of farce is this?

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.780
Why don't we take a short break?

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:49.030
We've been going at it all morning...

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:50.660
Yes, good idea.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.160
Marie, let's take a break.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.500
I can't.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:01.670
That would be a waste of time.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.170
I've got to get this right...

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.170
Get it right...

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:08.630
Otherwise, I can't
make any memories...

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:11.720
Hey!

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:12.930
Marie?

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.930
Are you okay?

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.560
I'm fine. It doesn't hurt.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.310
There's no way that
that doesn't hurt!

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:23.060
Hey, we're going to the infirmary.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.440
I said I was fine!

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:25.730
Yeah, but...

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:26.190
Marie-chan...

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.490
Marie, don't push yourself too hard.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:35.950
What do you think is the most
important thing for a pro to do?

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:41.330
It's to always make it
onstage in tip-top condition.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.630
Sudden illness, accidents...

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.460
No matter what the situation may
be, if you don't make it onstage...

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.130
You're a failure as a pro.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:56.470
Keep yourself in tip-top
condition and get onstage.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:13:00.890
If you can't do that, then there's no point,
no matter how hard you practice.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:07.230
Don't worry, Hanamura-senpai.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:10.360
Now that I've taken this on,
I'm going to give it my all.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:14.410
"Oh, I'll do my best..." I didn't
take this on lightly, all right?

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:19.370
I'm going to sing my heart out in front of
all the people who come to see us!

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:20.410
So you guys...

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.000
Let's give it everything
we've got till the end!

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.540
Oh, wow, there's a pro among us...

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:26.920
You said it.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:30.380
All right, then shall we
carry on a little longer?

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.170
Guess we're gonna have to.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.220
Marie-chan, are you gonna be okay?

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:35.760
Yes, I'll be okay.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:36.680
I can do this.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:38.930
All right, guys, let's do this!

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:39.930
Right!

00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:02.540
<i>Today I closed the deepest
part of my soul again</i>

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:08.750
<i>I want you to see, I don't want to
show it... A never-ending circle...</i>

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.710
Want to grab a bite
on our way home?

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:10.420
I'd like something that
I can eat while I'm jogging.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:12.960
Oh, so we have to
keep running in mind?

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:16.180
Those guys are working
pretty hard, huh?

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:17.260
Yeah.

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:19.720
I wish there was something
we could help with.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:21.850
Risette's doing a concert?

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.060
Seriously?

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:25.440
You mean she's gonna
go back to being an idol?

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.230
That's huge news!

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.030
That was pretty good,
don't you think?

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:35.030
It sounded passable!

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:37.160
Yes! We sounded good!

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:40.160
Then...

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.530
It's tomorrow, huh?

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:45.250
Crap! Now that it's really happening,
I'm getting nervous all of a sudden!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.370
You're getting spooked now?

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.630
If you're a man, then
you'll be lights out!

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:50.790
That's right!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.670
We're gonna be lights out!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.170
Yes. I'm sure we'll be fine.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.300
Right?

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:58.430
Not just "sure."

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:00.720
We're absolutely going to be fine.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.220
You guys!

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.100
It's okay to be nervous.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:10.440
Because there's a certain power you can get from
concerts that makes even getting nervous fun!

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:12.980
Don't think you have to do it perfectly.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.360
The audience wants to
have fun, you know.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.950
So we should be having fun first!

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:23.580
All right, let's go!

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.450
Let's thank our fans, our
friends, and ourselves!

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.460
Complete combustion!
One-shot victory!

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.460
All together...

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.960
Yeah!

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:58.360
Hurry up and bring it over!
We're out of time!

00:15:58.360 --> 00:15:59.530
Yes, sir!

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:01.990
Rise-chan sure is late.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:03.200
Damn her!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:06.040
After acting so cocky,
what the hell's she doing?

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:09.460
What's going on, Rise?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:10.670
Did something happen?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.790
<i>Senpai! Help me!</i>

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:13.500
<i>At this rate, I...</i>

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.920
<i>What should I do? I won't
make it to the concert!</i>

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.470
Rise-chan, you there?

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.050
Let us see your face!

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:23.300
There's a whole crowd of
people in front of my house...

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:26.100
Looks like someone launched
a false rumor on the net

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.810
about me doing a comeback
concert and meet-and-greet.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:32.310
<i>I can't leave my house
with that crowd here!</i>

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:35.020
They're all people who want to
see your concert, right?

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:37.150
So why don't you invite
them to come over here?

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:38.400
We can't do that!

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:42.070
We already handed out all of the numbered
tickets for the show this morning.

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:45.160
If they find out that they can't
see it even if they come over...

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:47.580
They might start a riot, huh?

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:50.460
And if that happens, the sale
goes right out the window!

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:52.000
Jeez!

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.080
Anything but that!

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.290
What should we do?

00:16:58.170 --> 00:16:59.800
I've got an idea.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.880
How long are you gonna
keep us waiting?

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.260
Can you get this thing
started, Risette?

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.470
No meet-and-greet yet?

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:08.640
Risette, we know you're there!

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.600
Hey! Look over there!

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.980
Fancy seeing Risette
in a place like that!

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.650
It's Risette!

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:21.360
Wait up!

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:24.110
I'm leaving the rest to you!

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.290
There's so many people.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:31.540
Yeah.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:34.670
You're getting spooked now, Senpai?

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:35.460
But...

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.840
For now... Let's have
some faith and wait.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:38.840
Yeah.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:42.920
Dad, hurry!

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.680
I've still got some
work to do, you know!

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:48.180
Yu gave you a ticket, didn't he?

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.770
I have a right to choose, too...

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.140
When is this thing gonna start?

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.060
How long are you
gonna make us wait?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.070
No good. She's not picking up.

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:02.780
I can't get a hold of Chie, either.

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.110
What are we gonna do?

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:06.160
We can't keep them
on ice much longer.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.330
But what can we do
without Ms. Kujikawa?

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:22.420
What do you think is the most
important thing for a pro to do?

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:25.430
You guys! Let's give it
everything we've got till the end!

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:33.350
Marie...

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:36.350
She's definitely coming. So...

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.480
That's right.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:39.860
Let's believe.

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.070
You guys...

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:47.990
Let's go!

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:07.260
<i>Even if I ignore my uneasiness,
my heart feels blue</i>

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:13.260
<i>In the end, another morning
when I feel lost will dawn again</i>

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:19.560
<i>If all I do is feel, I won't reach you</i>

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.730
<i>Change yourself...</i>

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:24.320
<i>Leave it up to the gods</i>

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:25.570
<i>Can't do that!</i>

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:31.410
<i>Just Find... The truth is I could hear it</i>

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:34.540
<i>Your sad voice,</i>

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:37.410
<i>all this time</i>

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:39.370
<i>Shake hands</i>

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:43.380
<i>Holding hands with courage...</i>

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.550
<i>Now, the stars</i>

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:50.430
<i>Are turning into a constellation</i>

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:51.800
<i>Shout Friends</i>

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:56.220
<i>Just the words that we mean...</i>

00:19:56.220 --> 00:20:02.440
<i>Let them echo all the way
to the ends of the earth!</i>

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:04.150
<i>Ring Bells!</i>

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:08.190
<i>The sound of our bells</i>

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:11.490
<i>Will begin opening</i>

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.620
<i>the door to tomorrow</i>

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:16.950
<i>True Story</i>

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:40.890
Encore! Encore!

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:44.060
Hey, I'm getting all fired up!

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:50.070
This is the real thrill of a concert!
Good thing I did my homework!

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.110
Stupid Teddie...

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:50.070
He's in no shape to perform.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.530
We're going next, right?

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:53.570
Of course!

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:54.410
All right!

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.490
Let's show them how real men do it!

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:02.830
They're too good... at dodging.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:05.540
Men can't stand on their faces, huh?

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.840
Never knew that.

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.590
Cheers!

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:15.350
You guys, thanks a lot! I'm saved!

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:18.060
Thanks to you, the sale was
a huge success, too!

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:20.270
Well, it doesn't sit well with me!

00:21:20.270 --> 00:21:22.600
Why did I have to
dress up like a girl?

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:25.190
But you said you wanted
to help them out.

00:21:25.190 --> 00:21:27.400
Not like this, I didn't!

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.280
Thanks, Ichijo-kun!

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.950
As a cross-dresser,
you looked like the real thing!

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:37.080
What's up with him?

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.870
I guess he felt like running?

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.120
He's an athlete, after all.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:43.960
Marie?

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:47.250
Were you able to create a memory?

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.880
Hey, I forgot.

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:53.340
Because I was so into it...

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:55.140
Well, that's pretty normal.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:59.060
It's because you can get so absorbed
that it becomes a memory later.

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.140
That's right.

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:02.680
Seeing you as a pretty
vocalist, Marie-chan...

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:05.560
That's totally burned
into my memory!

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:08.060
You moron!

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:11.570
I'm not gonna say
"hello, goodbye," okay?

00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:14.070
I'm all sweaty, I'm going to cool off.

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:30.090
What's this...

00:22:30.380 --> 00:22:31.590
From down there?

00:22:36.590 --> 00:22:39.350
Hey, hey... Big Bro and the others
were really cool, weren't they?

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:40.390
Yes, they were.

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:41.470
You think?

00:24:18.530 --> 00:24:20.160
This is all your fault.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:23.450
There's no profit or loss involved
when you're helping each other out.

00:24:23.450 --> 00:24:25.580
Help each other out... Right.

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:26.540
You must be lonely.

00:24:26.540 --> 00:24:28.080
Shut up! Shut up!

00:24:28.080 --> 00:24:29.290
Shut your mouth!
